    "created_at": "2021-10-11T20:34:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-11T20:34:33Z",
    "body": "I see. Not exposing the method at all is also divergence from path-to-regexp tooling though. I guess an option on `toRegExp` for whether or not to used named groups is not considered nice API design?\r\n\r\nMy imagined use case is being able to maintain a list of routes in a `URLPattern` compatible format, and through a web interface allow things like testing if a path matches a pattern, and copying the regexp for a pattern for usage in other tools. ",
